                        ],
                        "form": "embrowning"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "97190940-ddf0-439a-b52c-73d634fe67d7",
                        "entry_id": "7f2646cf-37ea-32d8-aab4-52c2dd2f1e20",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "embrowned"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                        "entry_id": "7f2646cf-37ea-32d8-aab4-52c2dd2f1e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make (something) brown; to brown."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "literary",
                            "poetic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b95c798-c80e-4217-8f44-90a8ff5538d1",
                                "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                                "text": "For time ſhall with his ready pencil ſtand; / Retouch your figures with his ripening hand; / Mellow your colors, and imbrown the teint; / Add every grace, which time alone can grant; / To future ages ſhall your fame convey, / And give more beauties than he takes away."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "864b9c98-2794-4085-8f55-927361fd526b",
                                "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                                "text": "For blight of the season embrowneth the bloom, / And time winnows falshood, like chaff, as it flies: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b805314-6e1e-4ce6-89a4-34afa40f0510",
                                "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                                "text": "The mountain-moss by scorching skies imbrown'd, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "053d2584-b84f-4ec4-94a7-6a15b99dad7c",
                                "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                                "text": "The heat embrowneth the harvests. They fall under the edge of the sickle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d23ea03a-fdb3-4f29-9d02-31a61e68f5dc",
                                "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                                "text": "His features were small, well formed, and delicate, though deeply embrowned by the eastern sun, and terminated by a flowing and curled black beard, which seemed trimmed with peculiar care."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14c15c5e-252c-4f8d-92d8-f7168fa7d852",
                                "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                                "text": "His fair hair waved long and freely over a white and unwrinkled forehead: the life of a camp and the suns of Italy had but little embrowned his clear and healthful complexion, which retained much of the bloom of youth."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c73c380-b914-43b1-9491-5020c5b7bbd8",
                                "sense_id": "db39e6f4-a11d-3c25-aab1-b66eb03cd292",
                                "text": "He was looking quite a different man to what I had left him; embrowned, sparkles in his eyes, so languid before."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37dfd828-349a-3bfb-9c5b-f6beb9924a50",
                        "entry_id": "7f2646cf-37ea-32d8-aab4-52c2dd2f1e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make (something) dark or dusky (“having a rather dark shade of colour”); to brown, to darken."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "literary",
                            "poetic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9e5bd508-e6be-40ca-acc1-1b064db2891f",
                                "sense_id": "37dfd828-349a-3bfb-9c5b-f6beb9924a50",
                                "text": "[…] Nature boon / Powrd forth profuſe on Hill and Dale and Plaine, / Both where the morning Sun firſt warmly ſmote / The open field, and where the unpierc't ſhade / Imbround the noontide Bowrs: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "75314b3e-f8e2-42d5-a6fb-6533b8ebb51c",
                                "sense_id": "37dfd828-349a-3bfb-9c5b-f6beb9924a50",
                                "text": "And thy dark Pencil, Midnight! darker ſtill / In Melancholy dipt, embrovvns the vvhole."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "970998b7-6167-4320-b34e-7e99decb9178",
                                "sense_id": "37dfd828-349a-3bfb-9c5b-f6beb9924a50",
                                "text": "No deeper clouds the grove embrowned, / No nether thunders shook the ground; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef71d56d-e67d-3b74-97b3-147794117328",
                        "entry_id": "7f2646cf-37ea-32d8-aab4-52c2dd2f1e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To become or make brown; to brown."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "intransitive",
                            "literary",
                            "poetic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "40bbc3d7-28fc-443b-b59b-8e7de9388efc",
                                "sense_id": "ef71d56d-e67d-3b74-97b3-147794117328",
                                "text": "[O]n the board diſplay'd / The ready meal before Ulyſſes lay'd. / (VVith flour imbrovvn'd) next mingled vvine yet nevv, / And luſcious as the Bee's nectareous devv: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d15bd96f-f2c6-452a-bc2a-53a3527be47b",
                                "sense_id": "ef71d56d-e67d-3b74-97b3-147794117328",
                                "text": "A greater opening ofttimes hedges up / With but a little forkful of his thorns / The villager, what time the grape imbrowns, […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ed168703-d61a-3d2d-bc5a-e2e3729915b7",
                        "entry_id": "7f2646cf-37ea-32d8-aab4-52c2dd2f1e20",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To become or make dark or dusky; to brown, to darken."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "intransitive",
                            "literary",
                            "poetic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b0f40fa-8eae-43a5-b77d-82ed0e203446",
                                "sense_id": "ed168703-d61a-3d2d-bc5a-e2e3729915b7",
                                "text": "Under theſe Auſpices, Jamblicus compoſed the Book juſt before mentioned, Of the Mytſeries; meaning the profound and recondite Doctrines of the Egyptian Philoſophy: VVhich, at Bottom, is nothing elſe but the genuine Greek Philoſophy, imbrovvned vvith the Fanaticiſm of Eatſern Cant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48bfafea-8e14-4f16-98ff-7e22052cddfc",
                                "sense_id": "ed168703-d61a-3d2d-bc5a-e2e3729915b7",
                                "text": "Now was the day departing, and the air, / Imbrown'd with shadows, from their toils releas'd / All animals on earth; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e2fd6975-09b7-44b3-b10d-c9d3e9a3f740",
                        "source_entry_id": "7f2646cf-37ea-32d8-aab4-52c2dd2f1e20",
                        "source_sense_description": "to make (something) brown — see also brown",
                        "target_lang_word": "embrunir",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "embrunir",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f46c60f-0620-3104-9c06-efbdfb1e2129",
                                        "entry_id": "1584e053-216f-3d08-a061-acd7c880d9b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Rendre brun ou plus brun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84bf5e73-e358-4068-a715-88c05a50cb47",
                                                "sense_id": "4f46c60f-0620-3104-9c06-efbdfb1e2129",
                                                "text": "Et moi seul j'aurai vu se lever cette aurore\nDans la tiède fraîcheur d'un matin embruni."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73cb028f-ce99-4213-bc03-3a7f8b8d7d65",
                                                "sense_id": "4f46c60f-0620-3104-9c06-efbdfb1e2129",
                                                "text": "Là, le raisin embrunissait dans les vignes basses, à cause de l’eau qui était tombée."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1776c4b0-2e48-37ef-920f-0782070b67b0",
                                        "entry_id": "1584e053-216f-3d08-a061-acd7c880d9b8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Devenir brun ou plus brun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pronominal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72087856-fcec-407b-ae00-2da4c884488d",
                                                "sense_id": "1776c4b0-2e48-37ef-920f-0782070b67b0",
                                                "text": "Puis il reprit sa route, car maintenant, au haut de la montée, dans l’ovale des frondaisons, s’embrunissait la perle humide et dorée du soir."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
